  "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=f(5x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $5.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218944/assets/f8bd94b2652d96417690f4ddb67a3d6c3235dd828c98b9f0ddebf0cf2fb13c51.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
